{
  "name": "fleshfly",
  "_about": "A fleshfly -- the flesh fly (Sarcophaga carnaria), 14 mm long: a big grey fly, the thorax with three black stripes, the abdomen chequered grey and black like a board (the squares shifting with the light), its tip red; red eyes set wide apart with a silvery face between; long black bristles all over; black legs with big pads on the feet; clear wings held back in a V. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/flies.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait; the wings at rest laid back over the abdomen, swung out and beating in the variant \"flying\").",
